Edits of the camera focal length and aperture with a host framing, see test_2819 and #2819

A sphere is rendered with a film translate framing sent by the host. The focal length, then the film aperture of the
camera are edited and restored: the film must scale around the center of the display window, the framing being kept.
The scenario only runs with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last one is compared against the
reference image.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
